ose up but  he says I think that down on the on the  time people understand it's just gonna  look like a silver shoe and as soon as  he said silver shoe I immediately  thought I want my shoe to be gold the  gold shoes was was clearly two things it  was it was a marketing statement by Nike  cause it was cause he was but also it  was a statement for Mike  saying I'm taking on this double and I'm  gonna do it sprinters are like  heavyweight boxers you take your ego you  take your confidence and if you make a  mistake you're on the map if I don't win  gold the fact that I'm wearing gold  shoes will be the least significant of  the issues the 400 meters was first and  you know and I was always aware that you  know that's the race that I don't win  this one then the whole double ideas is  out the window the Olympic final is like  no other race because you understand the  magnitude of it you know that if you get  it wrong for the wait four years four  years a long time to make well a big  history Michael must first  I'll never forget the amount of flash  bulbs that were going on I've never seen  anything  I would be kidding myself and lying to  everybody if I said that any point in  that race that I think that I was going  to be Michael Johnson no and nor did  anybody else in that race I can tell you  that  when I cross the finish line I think I  was just a little bit business as usual  it was very clear to me that Michael was  not in the moment Michael was still very  focused and and and very serious I think  he noticed that I was already focused on  the 200 it must be hard for Michael  because because he had the pressure of  of expectation on him to do the double  and he was already thinking about the  200 meters we're halfway there  this is real the pressure on this man  now is that playing on his mind I was  always aware of the fact that the 200  meters was going to be the most  difficult Jones and then in Lane 4 there  is I never ran the perfect race every  race had something where I didn't  execute it quite as I wish  I got a great reaction to the gun that  day so good that I actually wasn't quite  ready for it and ended up stumbling on  the third step out of the block he was  in such a hurry to get up to his top  speed that his foot almost missed the  ground I probably lost 200 for the  second there but I was able to recover I  was on the outside and as a result  Michael had to sort of come by me to get  past the key was always going to be for  me to get out around the curve and come  off of the bend on to the straight with  a lead  you know when you're on pace and on  track for world record and I could tell  that I was all I saw was the bow shoes  and a blur go by me  that night in Atlanta the world record  on home soil in the bowl shoes it's just  the defining moment of his career I  never thought I was a gamble I thought  what I proved to the world what I knew  that I could do
 

